For a 2D strategy game, a 400x200 pixel horizontal background image for the tech tree node "Calendar". A clean, moderately realistic animated art style set in Ancient Egypt. The perspective is a dynamic, low-angle shot looking up at the base of a towering stone obelisk that acts as a giant sundial. The shadow of the tip cuts perfectly across a series of large, white stone markers laid out in the plaza below. The atmosphere is sun-drenched and epic, emphasizing the mathematical mastery of time.


A 400x200 px background image for a game's tech tree card representing "Code of Laws". The aesthetic is Ancient Roman, featuring a clean, moderately realistic animated art style. The perspective is a low-angle shot focusing on the uniform of a Roman Lictor guard standing frozen at attention at the entrance of the Forum. He wears a clean white toga and grips a heavy, wooden-rod Fasces tightly in his hands. The background features the imposing, geometric architecture of Roman arches and pillars under a bright, clear sky, symbolizing the rigid structure of society under the law.


A 400x200 px horizontal tech tree icon for "Code of Laws" in a strategy game. The art style is a moderately realistic, animated illustration set in Ancient China. The scene features a close-up of a traditional bronze balance scale suspended in the air. On one side sits a heavy, standardized iron bell-weight stamped with the imperial insignia; on the other, a collection of goods perfectly balanced. The lighting is crisp and clear, hitting the bronze metallic surfaces. The image emphasizes precision, fairness, and the rigid, mathematical enforcement of state rules.


For a 2D Civ-like strategy game, a 400x200 pixel horizontal background image for the tech tree node "Construction". The style is Ancient Roman, moderately realistic, but clearly animated game art. The perspective is a dramatic, low-angle shot looking up at a massive stone aqueduct tier under construction. A colossal wooden treadwheel crane is lifting a heavy, hand-carved marble keystone into place at the crown of an arch. Roman engineers in tunics and leather tool belts stand on high wooden scaffolding, guiding the stone. The atmosphere is dusty and grand, with bright sunlight highlighting the texture of the raw stone blocks.


For a 2D Civ-like strategy game, a 400x200 pixel horizontal background image for the tech tree node "Currency". The style is Ancient Era, moderately realistic, but clearly animated game art. The composition is a sharp close-up of a dark, rustic wooden table piled with stacks and loose scatters of ancient Greek Tetradrachm and early Roman coins. The coins are thick, slightly irregular silver and gold discs, clearly stamped with high-relief profiles of gods, owls, and wheat. A single bronze balance scale rests slightly out of focus in the background. The lighting is warm and cinematic, catching the metallic glint and rough edges of the precious metal.


A 400x200 px horizontal tech tree icon for the "Republic" technology. The art style is a moderately realistic, animated illustration set in the Roman Curia (Senate House). The perspective is a wide, low-angle shot looking across tiers of curved stone benches. Several Roman senators, wearing traditional togas with broad purple stripes (toga praetexta), are standing and gesturing passionately during a debate. The background features grand, unadorned Republican-era brick and marble architecture. The atmosphere is filled with political energy and civic duty, completely avoiding military elements.




